WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
What's up everybody, my name is Ohara.

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.160
And today I'm gonna share with you guys:

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.420
three (3) reasons why Haikyuu is amazing.

00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.820
Have you ever watched a show that, somehow,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.120
got you downright hooked on something,

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.100
you had no interest in at all?

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.640
Or even genuinely disliked?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:19.222
Well, you probably know where this story is going,

00:00:19.222 --> 00:00:20.720
but I'm gonna tell it anyway.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.000
Because that is exactly what happened to me-

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.160
when I first discovered Haikyuu.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:28.900
I mean not only did I not care for volleyball,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.760
but the bunch of times I was forced to play

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.660
during high school, I found the game..

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.940
painfully underwhelming.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:35.900
Usually going home with a bunch of

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.780
burning scrapes on all my knees and elbows.

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.580
And then, BOOM, a couple of nerdy years

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.240
and one (1) season of Haikyuu later,

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:44.540
I'm standing in the gym,

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:47.880
excited out of my mind to play some volleyball.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.000
How the hell did that happen?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.960
Now, I'm guessing that this story,

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.420
at least to some degree,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.340
might sound very familiar to you.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.960
And I think we all can agree,

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.340
that whenever a manga or anime manages to

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:02.080
spark such a sudden passion for something,

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:05.660
that we used to have no interest in before whatsoever,

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.360
it must be doing something very, very, right.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.740
So, if you're like me and you're wondering,

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.780
how the heck an anime about volleyball, above all things

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.600
became so widely popular and unbearably entertaining,

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.240
you came to the right place.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.140
Because in this video we'll be discussing:

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.260
the three (3) things that make Haikyuu,

00:01:24.260 --> 00:01:26.760
one of the Top Shounen of the new era.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.500
I would say, compared to your average Shounen anime,

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.420
Haikyuu does most things pretty well,

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:35.280
that a decent Shounen needs.

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:37.560
Like, having an appealing art style,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.540
Or having adequate pacing.

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:42.300
With all of these things, Haruichi Furudate,

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.740
the author of Haikyuu, does a pretty damn good job overall.

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:48.940
However, what really sets the story apart

00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.200
from the average Shounen anime, are three (3) things,

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.920
in which Haikyuu easily surpasses much of its competition.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.000
Which also allowed it to successfully run

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.600
in Shounen Jump magazine, for over eight years.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.340
These three (3) things are the spot-on use

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:07.200
of a completely polarizing protagonist duo,

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:10.160
it's perfectly crafted story structure,

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.140
and finally, the immense amount of realism

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.120
and research that Haruichi has put into his work,

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.940
to make the story feel as incredibly convincing

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:20.760
and intriguing as it is.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:24.780
So, let's start by taking a closer look

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.820
at the two heroes of our story.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.580
First of all, before we get into the two protagonists,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.960
I want to mention that, I believe Haikyuu

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.120
has a very strong character set-up in general.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.360
Over the course of the story,

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:38.840
we increasingly meet new teams,

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.160
with new characters and philosophies,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.660
and somehow, most, if not all of them,

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:45.640
are immensely well-developed

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:47.720
and easy to connect with.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.560
That being said, let's move on to our heroes.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:52.080
The main characters in Haikyuu

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.180
are the small, but hard-working, Hinata Shōyō.

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:59.820
As well as the talented, but socially awkward, Kageyama Tobio.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.940
Strictly speaking, the story focuses more on Hinata,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:06.360
as he follows the road of the typical Shounen Hero.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.940
However, Kageyama comes very close in importance,

00:03:08.940 --> 00:03:11.840
and enjoys a similar amount of screen-time.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:13.760
What makes this quite unlikely duo

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.640
such a fantastic premise for the story however,

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.380
..is exactly that.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:21.520
They are the exact opposite of each other.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:23.820
Hinata is incredibly charismatic,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:26.020
and easily forms relationships with teammates

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.760
and opponents alike.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.120
His biggest weakness are his lack in height,

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.860
as well as his inexperience, that he has to overcome

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:35.220
through hard work and training.

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.680
Kageyama on the other hand, has been blessed with

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.020
immense talent and instinct for the sport

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.720
and is one of the most promising young prodigies in the country.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:45.860
However, he lacks basic social skills,

00:03:45.860 --> 00:03:48.420
that isolates him from his teammates.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.520
As a result, Hinata and Kageyama have completely opposing character arcs.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:56.460
Where one has to become better and stronger on the court,

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.860
While the other has to become a better person

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:01.360
and learn how to form real friendships.

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:03.840
Two very popular themes of Shounen,

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.420
that Haruichi splits into two characters here.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.180
What both have in common however,

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.000
is their strong will to fight and work hard in order to grow.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.700
So, in essence,

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.840
Haikyuu is about these two ambitious young men,

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.240
with opposing strengths and weaknesses,

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.360
that strive to become the best volleyball players in the country,

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:26.200
by learning from each other and growing together.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.040
One, striving to become stronger

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.200
and One to become a better person.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.900
The lesson here is that One can be successful

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:35.680
without the other, and this makes both of them

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:38.040
immensely easy to identify with

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.000
and makes us, want to see both of them succeed.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.840
Now the next thing we have to talk about is

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:49.240
Haikyuu's crazily perfected story structure.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.840
One of the most important criteria for a great Shounen story,

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.620
at least according to Hirohiko Araki,

00:04:55.620 --> 00:04:57.020
the author of JoJo's,

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:00.540
is that the protagonists are always rising, rising,

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:03.400
and yeah, you guessed it, rising again.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.440
But the reason why an always rising arc is so important

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:10.740
is that we always want to see the character keep progressing further.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.420
Even if he has his setbacks and low points,

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:16.620
the overall development always points upwards,

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.740
towards being a bit better than the last chapter.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.260
To better visualize this point, imagine a manga:

00:05:22.260 --> 00:05:25.420
where the hero is weak and friendless at the beginning.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:27.760
Nothing too uncommon, right?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.280
However, if he never gets any better,

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:32.100
no matter how hard he tries,

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:34.280
it would be kind of depressing to keep watching

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:36.580
this person's eternal struggle, right?

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.080
No.

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:38.480
What we want to see in Shounen,

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.960
is how our heroes succeed and grow,

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.840
and finally manage to be that one annoyingly arrogant guy.

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:47.800
There always is an annoyingly arrogant guy.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:48.980
As you might have guessed,

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:53.840
Haikyuu has brought this "always rising structure" to absolute perfection.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.720
The story starts with Hinata being the only person on his volleyball team during Middle School.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:01.380
Not even having the chance to have proper practice,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:04.620
but having to force his friends to toss him balls.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.560
From there the story progresses,

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.840
from finally joining Karasuno High,

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:10.300
the former school of his idol,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.440
over playing at the Inter-High, then the Spring High,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.920
all the way to the Tokyo Nationals.

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.800
Despite having to face progressively harder challenges along the way,

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.660
our heroes prevail in the end and keep fighting and growing.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:30.380
This gives the entire series a sense of continuous positive motion, that we all want to be a part of.

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:36.200
The reason that not more anime can pull off the tactic of the  "always rising arc" by using tournaments,

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:39.100
is, what do you do once the tournament is over?

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:45.940
And how do you come up with increasingly stronger and stronger opponents for the heroes without becoming too repetitive?

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:52.120
Haikyuu solves these two quite common problems by ending the series once a true high point has been reached.

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:57.700
And, more importantly maybe, is that Haruichi lets his antagonists grow as well,

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.720
and have them be a natural part of the journey.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:06.180
Rival teams, like Nekoma or Aoba Johsai, grow alongside the Karasuno team.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:10.460
And additionally, we might have opponents that might not be as strong as Karasuno,

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:16.660
But have unique tactics or a unique setup, with which they can pose a true threat to Hinata and Kageyama.

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:19.580
Everything in the story's development feels organic,

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:22.500
and that already brings me to my final point:

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.000
Setting.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:30.280
So, what's so super exciting about the setting in Haikyuu?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.100
I mean, it's pretty much our normal world, right?

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:38.160
We have Japanese High Schools: with teams that play volleyball in tournaments.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.960
No crazy magical powers.

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.680
No furries. No nothing.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.260
Well, let me tell you that it's,

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.460
actually, exactly the seamlessness of the Haikyuu world,

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.860
that makes it so good to watch.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:55.920
The level of realism and naturalness that Haruichi creates, is what fully emerges the reader..

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:57.060
So, us..

00:07:57.060 --> 00:07:58.340
..into the story.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:01.720
and that's what sparks this level of passion for the sport.

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:06.500
He has, without any doubt, sunk hours over hours into research about his story.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.220
From the basic rules and techniques of the game,

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:12.180
over the structures of Japanese High School volleyball,

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:16.380
all the way to the history and organization of the Clubs themselves.

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:20.440
This includes pretty mundane stuff you probably never thought about... Like,

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:23.000
How many referees are there at each tournament?

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.200
Or how do the uniforms have to look?

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:29.260
Or, how does the sports club actually finance itself?

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.660
All these things are just.. there..

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.800
and make it easy for you to lose yourself in the story.

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:37.700
But, if these things hadn't been thought about properly-

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:41.000
the plot would surely have been very different.

00:08:41.000 --> 00:08:43.360
Can you imagine watching a sports anime,

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.640
where the techniques aren't correct?

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:51.980
You'll always know something is kind of off and especially so if you actually like the sport itself.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.320
So, I guess my point here is:

00:08:54.320 --> 00:08:58.500
For amazing anime, the devil truly lies in the detail.

00:08:58.500 --> 00:09:01.160
And Haikyuu does a damn good job at it.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:08.420
So good even, that professional player: Kim Yeon-koung, praised the accuracy of the anime in a review on her personal YouTube channel,

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:13.740
Noting, that the creator of the series, must be a person with high level of volleyball knowledge.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:16.920
So, if a Pro is able to enjoy the show to its fullest,

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:20.280
it's no real surprise that we can as well.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:25.680
So, to recap: What makes Haikyuu stand out among so many others Shounen anime today?

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:29.980
It has an incredibly intriguing and fun protagonists duo.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.500
It has a constantly rising story structure,

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:37.300
in which we see Hinata, Kageyama and really almost everyone else in the show,

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:41.144
work incredibly hard to become better players and better people,

00:09:41.144 --> 00:09:42.640
which, let's face it,

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.600
is just ridiculously entertaining to watch.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:52.180
And finally, the story world is researched and created in so much detail and with so much dedication-

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:55.580
that it's really hard not to become involved in it.

00:09:55.580 --> 00:10:02.920
These three (3) extraordinarily well-executed things, are what make Haikyuu a true Top Shonen of the new era.

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:09.960
And, goddamn, now I really want to go out and play, but you know, you can't. So, that's it for today guys.

